WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Card Authorization & Reconciliation Lab
A guided look at recorded PostgreSQL tests. Synthetic funds; no live backend.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
01 / Capture creates an obligation
100 authorized. A partial capture makes 60 payable and leaves 40 held.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Expiry releases the remaining hold
40 returns to available capacity. The 60 already payable stays payable.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
A valid late clearing still posts
The remaining 40 clears after expiry. Payable reaches 100; the journal explains why.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Reusing released capacity can create exposure
In this variant, a later purchase uses capacity. Late clearing exposes a 30-unit shortfall.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
02 / A lost response leaves uncertainty
The process dies after commit. The app keeps the hold until authoritative evidence arrives.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Recovery releases the reservation once
The processor decline resolves uncertainty. Replaying recovery adds no financial effect.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
03 / Equal totals can hide different transactions
This deliberate identity-substitution fixture totals 100 on both sides, yet two rows differ.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Inspect the guarantees and their limits
Explore the architecture, crash tests and measured limits, including recovery backlog.
